    "raw": "Given:\n- Tim learns 10 words a day.\n- In 2 years, the number of words he knows increases by 50%.\n- We need to find the original number of words he knew.\n\nFirst, calculate the total number of days in 2 years:\n- Assuming a non-leap year has 365 days, 2 years would have \\(2 \\times 365 = 730\\) days.\n\nNext, calculate the total number of words Tim learns in 2 years:\n- He learns 10 words a day, so in 730 days, he learns \\(10 \\times 730 = 7300\\) words.\n\nThis 7300-word increase represents a 50% increase in the number of words he originally knew. Let \\(x\\) be the original number of words he knew. The increase of 50% means:\n\\[ 0.5x = 7300 \\]\n\nSolve for \\(x\\):\n\\[ x = \\frac{7300}{0.5} = 14600 \\]\n\nSo, Tim originally knew 14600 words.\n\nFINAL: 14600",
